==English==

===Etymology===
{{borrowed}} from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{term|ablator|ablātor|one that removes|lang=la}}, from {{term|ablatus|lang=la}}, suppletive past participle of {{term|auferre|auferō|to remove|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{a|US}} {{IPA|/æ.ˈbleɪd.ɚ/|/æ.ˈbleɪd.ə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# that which ablates (undergoes [[ablation]])
# {{astronautics}} a heat shield (which ablates during [[reentry]])

